@startuml
title 33. Queue System — Multi-Node Deployment

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

box "Node A" #LightBlue
participant "Worker A1" as WA1
participant "Worker A2" as WA2
participant "Recovery A" as RA
end box

box "Node B" #LightGreen
participant "Worker B1" as WB1
participant "Worker B2" as WB2
participant "Recovery B" as RB
end box

database "PostgreSQL\n(sync_jobs)" as DB
database "Redis\n(queues + locks)" as Redis

== Lock Contention Between Nodes ==

note over WA1, WB1: Both nodes compete for the same job via BRPOP

WA1 -> Redis: BRPOP :queue (gets job for app-X)
activate WA1
WA1 -> Redis: SETNX lock:app-X:tx_sync = "node-a-worker-1"
Redis --> WA1: OK (acquired)
WA1 -> DB: MarkStarted (WHERE status='pending')
WA1 -> Redis: SET heartbeat:{jobID}

WB1 -> Redis: BRPOP :queue (gets DIFFERENT job for app-X)
activate WB1
WB1 -> Redis: SETNX lock:app-X:tx_sync = "node-b-worker-1"
Redis --> WB1: FAIL (lock held by node-a-worker-1)

note right of WB1: Check heartbeat of lock holder

WB1 -> Redis: EXISTS heartbeat:{active-job-ID}
Redis --> WB1: 1 (alive — heartbeat present)
WB1 -> WB1: Backoff 5s → re-enqueue job
WB1 -> Redis: LPUSH :queue {job}
deactivate WB1

== Crash Recovery Across Nodes ==

note over WA1: Node A crashes!\n(lock + heartbeat orphaned)
destroy WA1

note over RB: Recovery B runs periodic check (10 min interval)

RB -> DB: FindByStatus('processing')
DB --> RB: job on app-X (no heartbeat, started > 2 min)
RB -> Redis: EXISTS heartbeat:{jobID}
Redis --> RB: 0 (expired — Node A crashed)
RB -> Redis: DEL lock:app-X:tx_sync (ForceReleaseLock)
RB -> DB: MarkPendingIfProcessing (conditional)
RB -> Redis: LPUSH :queue {job}
note right of RB: Job now available for any worker on any node

== Lock Steal (Dead Worker Detection) ==

WB2 -> Redis: BRPOP :queue (picks up re-enqueued job)
activate WB2
WB2 -> Redis: SETNX lock:app-X:tx_sync = "node-b-worker-2"
Redis --> WB2: OK (lock was released by recovery)
WB2 -> DB: MarkStarted
WB2 -> Redis: SET heartbeat:{jobID}
WB2 -> WB2: Process job successfully
WB2 -> Redis: Lua: DEL lock IF value=="node-b-worker-2"
WB2 -> DB: MarkCompleted (WHERE status='processing')
deactivate WB2

== Ownership-Aware Lock Operations ==

note over WA2, WB2
  All lock operations use Lua scripts for atomicity:
  • ReleaseLockIfOwner: DEL only if value matches workerID
  • ExtendLockIfOwner: PEXPIRE only if value matches workerID
  • StealLock: check holder → DEL → SET NX (single script)

  This prevents:
  • Worker A releasing Worker B's lock after slow processing
  • Stale heartbeat extensions from zombied goroutines
  • Race conditions in lock steal between nodes
end note

@enduml
